The SVG backend, table_format.rs, and native parser subset come from
franken_markdown 0.7.0, https://crates.io/crates/franken_markdown/0.7.0,
upstream commit ddbdefd8c35770766838a735c554119ff0ef39e3.
LICENSE in this directory applies to these upstream files.
The published crate still supplies AST types, fonts, shaping primitives,
line-breaking primitives, and the diagram/math engines.

The local SVG changes add independent heading/code typography and colors.
Generated vector figures fill local content width at their original aspect
ratio. Ordinary images retain intrinsic sizing. Narrow pages reduce margins.
The painter records the same retained shaping clusters and physical line
advances that it paints, including ligatures, composition, code tab expansion,
table cells, and emergency wrapping. These coordinates start in SVG user units.
The native renderer converts them through the emitted viewBox, resolved usvg
dimensions, and raster scale into full-page raster pixels. Viewport overlays
subtract the actual clamped viewport scroll, without changing cached geometry.
Images, diagrams, and successfully typeset vector math are graphics, not text
clusters. Actual visible fallback text still has text geometry.

src/parse contains the pinned native grammar with source-provenance hooks.
It carries original UTF-8 source spans through accepted inline tokens,
entities, escapes, emphasis resolution, links, code normalization, containers,
tables, normalized line endings, host image fallback text, and endnote copies.
It does not reparse with another grammar, search source text for equal strings,
or infer source identity from text occurrence order. Source soft breaks become
source-owned logical spaces after the same native break recognition.
The parser's internal copied-prefix tracker also retains original tab columns.
The endnote adapter uses structural AST copy identities, including moved notes.
Layout pieces and words own explicit logical-byte maps through coalescing,
wrapping, tab expansion, and painting. Only document-owned AST leaves retain
address identities. Generated markers cannot inherit dropped word mappings.

vendor_parser.py reproduces the parser subset from an unmodified 0.7.0 src
directory. It requires Python 3 and Pygments only for regeneration, not builds.
Run: python vendor/franken-markdown/vendor_parser.py /path/to/franken_markdown-0.7.0/src
The script checks SHA-256 of the original parser and an ordered digest of all
original helper inputs before extraction. It excludes upstream test fixtures,
CLI entry points, external profiling APIs, HTML lowering/sanitizing, and
page-note/heading metadata paths. The private HTML URL-tokenizer closure remains
for the parser tracker. Local provenance modules are maintained beside it.
The generated source is checked in and ships under Cargo's existing vendor/**
include. No registry file is changed and no path dependency is required.

fmd-font/fonts/test-shaping/FmdShaping.ttf is from fmd-font 0.4.0,
https://crates.io/crates/fmd-font/0.4.0, and supports upstream SVG tests.
Each upstream license is included alongside its corresponding files.
